<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">House of Borgia</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Borja family</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The House of Borgia was a noble family of Valencian origin (Borja) that rose to great power in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/renaissance">Renaissance</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>. It produced two popes, Callixtus III (1455–1458) and Alexander VI (1492–1503), whose children Cesare and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lucrezia-borgia">Lucrezia Borgia</a> became notorious in politics and legend. Cesare's conquests in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/romagna">Romagna</a> collapsed after his father's death in 1503, while a later member, Francis Borgia, became a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jesuits">Jesuit</a> leader and saint.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/house-of-borgia.jpg" alt="House of Borgia" width="320" height="372" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: MostEpic · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Arms_of_the_house_of_Borgia_(1).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
